+# Epic Breakdown: Pulseboard
+
+**Project**: Pulseboard  
+**Date**: 2026-08-10  
+**Total Epics**: 3 (E000 plus 2 product epics)  
+**Estimated Total Stories**: 11-17
+
+---
+
+## Epic Dependency Map
+
+```text
+E000 Developer Infrastructure → E001 Reviewed Action Workflow → E002 Reminder Delivery & Pilot Evidence
+```
+
+## Epic Prioritization
+
+### MVP Epics (Must Have)
+
+- E000: Developer Infrastructure
+- E001: Reviewed Action Workflow
+- E002: Reminder Delivery & Pilot Evidence
+
+### Enhancement Epics (Should Have)
+
+- None in the bounded pilot plan.
+
+### Future Epics (Nice to Have)
+
+- Not planned. Meeting recording, calendar replacement, and autonomous outbound messaging are explicit non-goals.
+
+---
+
+## Epic Definitions
+
+### E000: Developer Infrastructure
+
+**Value Statement**: This epic gives the two-engineer pilot team a reliable way to test, build, configure, and observe the product before user-facing work begins.
+
+**Scope Summary**: Establish the Python API and browser UI development baseline: local lint/test/build commands, CI for documentation-appropriate code paths, environment configuration, and error observability. It does not select the reminder provider or implement product workflows.
+
+**Success Criteria**:
+
+- [ ] A developer can run the agreed lint, test, and build checks locally.
+- [ ] CI runs the relevant checks for product changes.
+- [ ] Environment configuration separates local and pilot values without committing secrets.
+- [ ] Pilot failures have enough error context to investigate.
+
+**User Stories Summary**:
+
+- Python API and browser UI project baseline.
+- Unit/integration test, lint, formatting, and build commands.
+- CI checks and environment configuration.
+- Error observability for the pilot.
+
+**Dependencies**:
+
+- **Depends On**: None.
+- **Enables**: E001, E002.
+
+**Touch-points (creates/modifies)**:
+
+- Migrations: —
+- Models/Services: application configuration and observability bootstrap
+- Files/Components: API/UI project configuration, CI workflows, test configuration, environment templates
+
+**Estimated Stories**: 3-5  
+**Priority**: P0 — Foundation  
+**Target Phase**: Phase 0
+
+---
+
+### E001: Reviewed Action Workflow
+
+**Value Statement**: This epic enables meeting facilitators to turn a transcript into workspace-safe, reviewed action items, so that no reminder can be scheduled from an unconfirmed proposal.
+
+**Scope Summary**: Build the primary pilot workflow: workspace-aware access, transcript upload, action proposal generation, and explicit facilitator confirmation of text, owner, and due date. This epic delivers PRM-001, PRM-002, and PRM-004; it does not send reminders.
+
+**Success Criteria**:
+
+- [ ] A facilitator can upload a transcript and review proposed action items.
+- [ ] Scheduling is unavailable until the facilitator confirms action text, owner, and due date.
+- [ ] A real request from another workspace cannot read the workspace’s transcripts or actions.
+- [ ] A facilitator LARP can complete the upload-to-confirmation experience.
+
+**User Stories Summary**:
+
+- Workspace principal and workspace-scoped transcript/action access.
+- Transcript upload and proposal presentation.
+- Proposal editing and explicit confirmation gate.
+- Proposed versus confirmed action state and review instrumentation.
+
+**Dependencies**:
+
+- **Depends On**: E000.
+- **Enables**: E002.
+
+**Touch-points (creates/modifies)**:
+
+- Migrations: workspace, transcript, action proposal, and confirmed action persistence (schema finalized in E001)
+- Models/Services: workspace request scoping, transcript ingestion, action proposal, confirmation workflow
+- Files/Components: transcript upload, action review, confirmation UI, workspace-scoped API routes
+
+**Estimated Stories**: 5-8  
+**Priority**: P0 — MVP critical  
+**Target Phase**: Phase 1
+
+---
+
+### E002: Reminder Delivery & Pilot Evidence
+
+**Value Statement**: This epic enables facilitators to send one reminder for a confirmed action and inspect its delivery status, turning reviewed actions into observable follow-through during the pilot.
+
+**Scope Summary**: Add a configurable reminder-provider adapter, one reminder delivery attempt per confirmed action, user-visible delivery status, and pilot-safe measurement for review and outcome metrics. The provider remains undecided until a later decision; E002 consumes E001’s frozen action and workspace schema.
+
+**Success Criteria**:
+
+- [ ] A confirmed action can trigger one reminder through the configured provider.
+- [ ] Delivery success or failure is recorded and visible to the facilitator.
+- [ ] Runtime evidence exercises upload → confirmation → delivery through the real selected provider path.
+- [ ] Pilot metrics capture review rate and allow the agreed overdue-action comparison.
+
+**User Stories Summary**:
+
+- Configurable reminder provider adapter and safe credentials handling.
+- One reminder attempt for a confirmed action.
+- Delivery status display and failure handling.
+- Pilot measurement events and reporting export/view.
+
+**Dependencies**:
+
+- **Depends On**: E000, E001.
+- **Enables**: Pilot outcome assessment.
+
+**Touch-points (creates/modifies)**:
+
+- Migrations: delivery-attempt/status and pilot-measurement fields only; no changes to E001 frozen shared tables without an explicit later decision
+- Models/Services: reminder provider adapter, delivery-status service, pilot metrics aggregation
+- Files/Components: reminder configuration, action delivery status, pilot metrics surface, provider integration routes
+
+**Estimated Stories**: 3-4  
+**Priority**: P0 — MVP critical  
+**Target Phase**: Phase 2
+
+---
+
+## Epic Execution Strategy
+
+### Phase 0: Developer Infrastructure
+
+**Goal**: establish a reliable development and evidence baseline.
+
+**Epics**: E000
+
+**Success Gate**: local checks and CI are available; pilot configuration and error observability are defined.
+
+### Phase 1: Reviewed Actions
+
+**Goal**: let a facilitator safely create confirmed actions from an uploaded transcript.
+
+**Epics**: E001
+
+**Success Gate**: the primary workflow satisfies PRM-001, PRM-002, and a real cross-workspace negative probe for PRM-004.
+
+### Phase 2: Reminder Delivery and Pilot Evidence
+
+**Goal**: deliver one confirmed reminder and prove the complete pilot path.
+
+**Epics**: E002
+
+**Success Gate**: the real upload-to-confirmation-to-delivery path and delivery status are evidenced for the selected provider.
+
+## Risk Mitigation by Epic
+
+| Epic | Primary Risk | Mitigation Strategy |
+|------|--------------|-------------------|
+| E000 | A rushed baseline leaves the pilot untestable | Make local checks, CI, and configuration explicit before feature work |
+| E001 | An unconfirmed or cross-workspace action is exposed | Enforce confirmation and request-role isolation; prove the negative path |
+| E002 | Provider uncertainty blocks pilot delivery | Isolate provider behind an adapter and represent failure honestly |
+
+## Success Metrics by Epic
+
+| Epic | Key Metric | Target | Measurement |
+|------|-----------|--------|-------------|
+| E000 | Relevant check path available | Local and CI checks exist before E001 | CI and developer walkthrough |
+| E001 | Proposal review rate | ≥80% during pilot | Proposal/review events |
+| E002 | Unowned overdue actions | 30% reduction after four weeks | Per-team baseline comparison |
+
+## Notes
+
+- This is a sequential three-epic plan; concurrency waves are not required for a Build project below the four-epic threshold.
+- The reminder provider choice remains open and is deliberately isolated to E002.
+- E001 owns the initial shared schema so E002 can consume a stable action/workspace boundary.
+
+---
